    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "GVM Auctioneers are delighted to present to the market this stunningly attractive four bedroom bungalow residence, superbly positioned on a beautifully appointed site extending to circa 0.75 statute acres in the highly desirable Belmont area of Castleconnell.\n\nThe property is approached via an impressive sweeping driveway, framed by a block built and plastered boundary wall, leading to a generous set down, parking and circulation area to the front. The mature grounds are a particularly appealing feature, incorporating beautifully manicured lawns complemented by colourful flower beds, established shrubbery and pleasant outdoor spaces.\n\nInternally, the residence offers bright, spacious and well-proportioned living and bedroom accommodation. The layout comprises a welcoming entrance hall, sitting room, TV room, kitchen/dining area, utility room with WC off, four generously sized bedrooms and a main bathroom. The accommodation is practical and versatile, making it ideally suited to the requirements of modern family living.\n\n A significant feature of the property is the substantial detached store, which benefits from separate access and an automated door. This excellent facility is ideally suited for use as a workshop, secure storage area or home office. It may also offer potential for conversion to a self contained residential unit, subject to obtaining the necessary planning permission.\n\nThe property benefits from mains sewerage, double glazed UPVC windows and oil-fired central heating.\n\nBelmont enjoys an outstanding location adjacent to the picturesque and much sought-after village of Castleconnell. Beautifully positioned on the banks of the River Shannon, the village offers scenic riverside walks together with an excellent range of amenities, including supermarkets, a renowned primary school, welcoming hostelries, restaurants and coffee shops.There is also a strong selection of sporting and recreational facilities nearby, including boating, soccer and GAA clubs.\n\n Despite its pleasant semi rural setting, the property enjoys excellent accessibility. The University of Limerick and Plassey Technological Park are within approximately ten minutes` drive, while Limerick City is readily accessible in approximately 20 minutes. Castleconnell also benefits from both rail and bus connections to Limerick City, together with convenient access to the M7 Motorway and the wider national road network.\n\nThis sensibly priced and exceptionally well located property represents an ideal opportunity for families, first-time buyers or those seeking a spacious home on a substantial mature site while also offering the tranquillity of a pleasant rural setting yet remaining within easy reach of the extensive amenities available in Castleconnell and Limerick City.\n\nViewing of this wonderful home is very highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall - 3.3m (10'10\") x 2.5m (8'2\")\nCarpet flooring.\nBuilt in storage presses.\n\nSitting Room - 8.2m (26'11\") x 3.6m (11'10\")\nFeature Fireplace.\nCarpet flooring.\nLarge Windows overlooking front garden\n\nKitchen/dining room - 6.3m (20'8\") x 3.01m (9'11\")\nTiled and Laminate flooring.\nEye and Floor level presses\n\n\nUtility Room - 3.1m (10'2\") x 1.7m (5'7\")\nGenerous presses and built in sink.\n\n\nSitting room - 6.7m (22'0\") x 3m (9'10\")\nCarpet flooring\n\nBathroom - 2.5m (8'2\") x 2m (6'7\")\nFully fitted and tiled\n\nBedroom 1 - 2.5m (8'2\") x 2.4m (7'10\")\nDouble.\nCarpet flooring.\nBuilt in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.8m (12'6\") x 2.8m (9'2\")\nDouble.\nCarpet flooring.\nBuilt in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.7m (12'2\") x 3m (9'10\")\nDouble.\nCarpet flooring.\nBuilt in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 4\nDouble.\nCarpet flooring.\nBuilt in wardrobes.\n\nDetached Store/Workshop - 15m (49'3\") x 7.7m (25'3\")\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
